abstract: >-
  Finding raster data (historical maps, declassified CORONA imagery,
  Sentinel-2 and SRTM elevation data) and analyzing digital elevation models
  in QGIS (slope, aspect, hillshade and classification). This module was
  taught as part of the Purdue-NSF GIS Cybertraining for the Social Sciences
  Workshop, a two-day workshop held at Purdue University in 2026, to GIS
  professionals and instructors (Day 1, Session A QGIS track, part 2).
